### 7.2 The Energy-Size Proof

The zero-point energy per gauge boson is:

$$E_z = m_z c^2 = 6.629432672 \times 10^{-34}\,\mathrm{J}$$

The energy density of the vacuum — energy per unit gauge area — is:

$$\sigma = \frac{E_z}{A_q} = \frac{m_z c^2}{\lambda_q^2/\sqrt{3}} = \frac{m_z c^2 \sqrt{3}}{\lambda_q^2}$$

